<p>The code defines endpoints for:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>POST /sensors</code>: This endpoint creates a new sensor by providing the sensor type, description, and location.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>POST /sensor_data/{sensor_id}</code>: Streams sensor data for a specific sensor. The data can be a single point or a batch.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><code>GET /daily_avg/{sensor_id}</code>: Retrieves daily statistics (average, min, max, median, IQR) for the given sensor over the last 7 days.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>In the query for the sensor statistics, the data is able to be partitioned quickly with Timescale&#x27;s <code>time_bucket()</code> function by using the indexes generated when you created the hypertable. Likewise, you can easily calculate things like the interquartile range (IQR) using Timescale-specific functions.</p>
